# Implementation Plan: Deploying IT Inventory to DeanOS

This plan outlines the steps to replace the current IT Inventory installation on the DeanOS server (`192.168.1.186`) with the updated "premium" version from the local workspace.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The deployment will involve restarting the `it-inventory` Docker container on the server. This will result in a brief downtime (approx. 30-60 seconds).
>
> [!WARNING]
> We will be syncing the `/DATA/dean/projects/My-Personal-Repository/` directory on the server. A full backup will be created before any changes are applied.

## Proposed Changes

### Phase 1: Server Cleanup (Destructive)

#### [TASK] Stop & Remove Container
- SSH into DeanOS.
## Deployment Plan

1.  **Cleanup & Sync (Local):** Verify local files are clean and in sync with `main`.
2.  **Server Preparation (DeanOS):**
    *   Clean up existing project directory and container on `192.168.1.186`.
    *   Clone the repository to `/DATA/dean/projects/My-Personal-Repository/`.
3.  **Deployment (DeanOS):**
    *   Navigate to `/DATA/dean/projects/My-Personal-Repository/`.
    *   Set correct permissions: `sudo chown -R dean:samba .`.
    *   Run build: `sudo docker compose up -d --build it-inventory`.
4.  **Verification:**
    *   Confirm container is running: `sudo docker ps`.
    *   Test "Add New Device" and "Add Request" buttons.

## UI Responsiveness Investigation

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The user reports that the "Add New Device" and "Add Request" buttons are unresponsive.

1.  **Check for JS Errors:** Inspect the browser console for script loading failures or runtime errors.
2.  **Verify Script Inclusion:** Ensure Bootstrap and local scripts are correctly loaded in `base.html`.
3.  **Analyze Z-Index/Overlays:** Check if the premium glassmorphism effects (e.g., `.bg-glow`, high navbar z-index) are unintentionally blocking clicks.
4.  **Test in Container Environment:** Verify if the issue is specific to the production environment (deployment issues) or present in the local codebase.

